{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>However, on the fifteenth day of the seventh month, when you gather.</b> One should ask here: was it not already stated above, ״בחמשה עשר יום לחדש השביעי הזה חג הסכות״? But this is the way of Scripture, on account of the length of the subject matter and all that it interpolated in between. And it further appears to me to say that above it mentioned the matter of the offerings, which are the statutes of the Blessed Name, and there it alludes to those above — this is what it said: ״on the first day a holy convocation, on the eighth day a holy convocation.״ But here, below, it will explain those below and mention the statutes of Israel — that they celebrate the festival of HaShem seven days at the time of gathering, and that they take in it the commandment of the lulav to atone for the corruption of our first father which occurred at this season. And this is why it immediately attached to it ״ולקחתם לכם״, and this appears correct to me."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The abbreviation הש\"י resolved as 'the Blessed Name' (השם יתברך), following the voice rules for reverent epithets."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:56.858476051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}